# The `Ssum` table of the certificate (data file)

`ssumTableL[i][j] = unpack (packedRow (mult (cSigs[i]).1)) (mult (cSigs[j]).1)`: the value of the
packed row DP of the `i`-th signature group (as row owner, i.e. the *second* argument of `Ssum`)
at the state of the `j`-th group, for `k = 50`.

The literal was computed by `Submission/numerics/gen_table.py`, an independent state-vector DP
validated against the machine-checked `Ssum` values of `Submission/Variational.lean`
(`Ssum [2] [2] 50 = 11000`, `Ssum [2,2] [2,2] 4 = 5856`, ...).  Its correctness in Lean is
established in `Submission.CertSsum.lean` by the packed row DP itself.
-/

